1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Meet the world's tiniest pencil.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,460
No lead. Just electrons.

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:08,900
A classic analog oscilloscope turns a
changing voltage into a line of light.

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:13,480
Inside its glass tube is an electron
gun: a little assembly that releases,

5
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,500
controls, accelerates
and focuses electrons.

6
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,680
Let us follow them.

7
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:22,655
First, the heater. In this common design,
a small filament warms a separate,

8
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:27,215
coated cathode. This is an indirectly
heated cathode: the heater supplies

9
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,375
warmth; the cathode supplies
the beam's electrons.

10
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,155
Heat gives some electrons enough energy
to escape the surface, a process called

11
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:38,175
thermionic emission. They were already
in the material; we have not invented new

12
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:42,295
electrons. Electrons arriving through
the cathode's electrical connection

13
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,180
replace those carried away by the beam.

14
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,795
Meanwhile, the tube's vacuum removes
nearly all the gas, allowing electrons to

15
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,280
travel with very few collisions.

16
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,535
Immediately ahead sits the control
grid, usually a small metal cup with an

17
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,540
opening. It is held negative
relative to the cathode.

18
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:02,220
Its electric field restricts how
many electrons can enter the beam.

19
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,380
Make it less negative, and more
pass through: a brighter trace.

20
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:09,180
Make it more negative,
and the beam dwindles.

21
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:10,600
At cutoff, it is stopped.

22
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,380
Nothing has to slide shut.

23
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,660
This electrical gate can
blank the beam between sweeps.

24
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:17,760
A remarkably punctual doorman.

25
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:23,755
Next, accelerating electrodes, called
anodes, establish voltages more positive

26
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:28,255
than the cathode. Their electric fields
give the electrons forward speed as they

27
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:29,600
pass through aligned openings.

28
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:34,695
'Positive' here means relative to the
cathode, not necessarily positive relative

29
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,740
to ground. The power supply
provides this energy.

30
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:41,995
The heater releases electrons from the
surface; these voltage differences do the

31
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:42,820
accelerating.

32
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:46,500
Speed alone would give us
a rather untidy splodge.

33
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:50,960
Shaped electrodes at carefully chosen
voltages create an electrostatic lens.

34
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:55,303
Its curved electric field bends the paths
of electrons towards a small spot on

35
00:01:55,328 --> 00:01:58,420
the screen, much as an optical
lens brings light to a focus.

36
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,700
There is no piece of glass in this lens.

37
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,900
Turn the focus control, and you
adjust its electrical strength.

38
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:08,355
Now the beam reaches two pairs of
deflection plates, arranged at right

39
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:12,875
angles. Because electrons carry negative
charge, they bend towards the more

40
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:16,600
positive plate. One pair steers
vertically; the other horizontally.

41
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,280
The input signal, suitably
amplified, drives the vertical pair.

42
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:23,900
As that voltage rises and falls,
the spot follows it up and down.

43
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:29,235
To spread that movement across time, a
ramp voltage sweeps the spot steadily

44
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:33,415
from left to right. During the rapid
return, called flyback, the beam is

45
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:38,275
blanked. At the screen, energetic
electrons excite a phosphor coating, which

46
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,420
emits light and briefly continues glowing.

47
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:44,020
The travelling spot and its
fading trail make the waveform.

48
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:48,240
Our drawn beam path is an illustration;
the light appears at the screen.

49
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:53,235
Finally, the trigger waits for a chosen
event, such as the signal crossing a

50
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,160
selected voltage in the rising direction.

51
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:59,535
Each sweep then begins at the same point
in a repeating signal, so the trace

52
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:03,780
settles. Height tells us voltage;
distance across tells us time.

53
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:08,060
An electron gun, some careful steering,
and rather lovely handwriting.
